  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nQuieter weather will move in on Tuesday, although some additional \nlow end (less than 25 percent) PoPs are then possible on Tuesday \nafternoon and evening as a weak trough pushes through the region. At \nthis point, not expecting much in the way of rainfall totals as any \nshower development will remain isolated in nature and mainly \nconfined to areas east of US-183. While some embedded thunderstorms \nmay also be possible with this Tuesday activity, current trends \ncontinue to keep the majority of the precipitation just to the east \nacross eastern Nebraska where the best instability will be located. \nTherefore, not anticipating any severe storms with this system. \nDrier conditions return mid-week as weak upper level ridging and \nsurface high pressure builds into the region. A return to scattered \nshowers is expected by late week and into the first half of next \nweekend, but confidence remains too low in development, timing, and \nstrength to put much more than a mention in the forecast at this \ntime. \n\nAs upper level ridging builds back into the region on Tuesday, warm \nair advection in combination with decreasing clouds will allow for \nwarmer temperatures to return through the end of the week. \nTemperatures will steadily rise back into the low to mid 60s Tuesday \nthrough Friday. Some locations along and south of the I-80 corridor \ncould even rise back into the 70s towards the end of the week. \nSlightly cooler temperatures (but still in the low to mid 60s) \nreturn on Saturday as precipitation chances return to the area.",
